<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i-1)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

However, the above assert statement is not quite correct based on the description. The correct assert statement should account for the fact that the element at the insertion point is shifted up, and the new element is placed at the insertion point. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

This ensures that for every valid index `i` from the insertion point to the previous size of the vector, the element at position `i+1` in the updated vector is equal to the element at position `i` in the old vector. The element at the insertion point `index` is the newly inserted element, so it doesn't need to be included in this loop.
