However, there seems to be a small mistake in the above assert statement. The correct assertion should account for the fact that the element at the `index` position is the newly inserted element, and all elements after that are shifted by one position. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert \forall int i; index < i && i <= \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>

This ensures that for every valid index `i` from `index + 1` to the previous size of the vector, the element at position `i` in the updated vector is equal to the element at position `i-1` in the old vector. The element at the `index` position is the newly inserted element, so it doesn't need to be included in this comparison.
